<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Min and max">
        <Paragraph>
            Use <Code>Min</Code> and <Code>Max</Code> to restrict the available dates. Month and year navigation buttons are disabled when their destination month falls entirely outside these limits. Keyboard paging respects the same limits.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            The month dropdown disables months outside the allowed range, and the year input uses the minimum and maximum years. Changing the year moves the calendar to the nearest allowed month when needed.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            This inline example allows dates from one month before today to one month after today. Navigate to either boundary month to see the corresponding month navigation button become disabled.
        </Paragraph>
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
